 E(64,"BD-169","divided_eruv","boundary_gap","moed","The Community's Divided Eruv",
   "[kbd_litigant_a.GetFirstName] says the courtyard's shared boundary was checked before the Sabbath. [kbd_litigant_b.GetFirstName] says a gap opened where carts pass. Families need to know whether they may carry between homes. The court must give clear guidance while the boundary's condition is established.",
   ["Declare the arrangement valid without inspection.","Inspect the cart passage and repair any gap.","Declare the whole arrangement invalid for this Sabbath."],
   ["Families can carry as planned, but a real gap would make the ruling unsafe.","Inspection costs time and supplies, yet settles the physical fact.","Strict caution is clear, but an intact boundary would make disruption needless."],
   ["The court confirms the eruv without walking the cart passage.","The court sends a qualified examiner to the passage and orders repair if needed.","The court tells every household to refrain from carrying this Sabbath."],
   "The cart passage has a break. A declaration made without seeing it was unsound.",
   "The boundary is continuous and maintained. Blanket invalidation burdened households without cause.",
   "Cite a mastered Moed work and inspect the boundary.",
   "Mishnah Eruvin 1:1 treats the construction of shared boundaries. A text cannot show whether this passage has a gap today.",
   "Have a scholar and steward walk the passage before the Sabbath.",
   "The judges make a physical check and give households timely guidance.",
   ["Uninspected approval risks substantial Stability.","Inspection and repair cost some Stability.","Blanket invalidation costs less now but may burden households needlessly."],
   "[CHARACTER.GetTitledFirstName] ruled on [TARGET_CHARACTER.GetFirstName]'s courtyard arrangement." ,"stability"),
